        <semantic:textAnnotation id="_1cd404a4-0dee-475d-89b9-5e136cb7c712">
            <semantic:text>Determine model based on data characteristics: Time Series Analysis, Exponential Smoothing, ARIMA, Regression Analysis, Machine Learning Models, Moving Averages, Croston Method</semantic:text>
        </semantic:textAnnotation>
        <semantic:textAnnotation id="_7483c5db-6d72-482b-a670-a76ae5413c93">
            <semantic:text>The following are a range of data characteristics organizations may need to account for when designing to-be demand forecasting processes:
Seasonality: Periodic fluctuations in demand (e.g., holidays, seasons)
Trend: Long-term movement in data (e.g., increasing or decreasing sales)
Cyclic Patterns: Repeating cycles not tied to a specific period
External Factors: Economic indicators, competitor actions, market conditions
Product Lifecycle Stage: Introduction, growth, maturity, decline
Promotional Activities: Marketing campaigns, discounts, promotions
Sales Channels: Online, offline, geographical locations
Customer Demographics: Age, gender, income, preferences
Lead Time: Time taken from order placement to delivery</semantic:text>
        </semantic:textAnnotation>
